{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And if to his son he designates her.</b> The master — this teaches that even his son stands in his stead to designate her if his father so wishes, and he need not betroth her with separate kiddushin, but says to her: 'Behold, you are designated to me through the money your father received in your redemption money.'" "<b>After the manner of daughters.</b> Food, clothing, and conjugal relations (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:28.160590234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}